column2:
The government has announced that it will be providing free VR equipment to social outcasts in an effort to help them reintegrate into society. This will be part of a "VR game therapy" program, where participants will be able to socialize and work together in a virtual space as a way to gently introduce themselves to society.
With this initiative, the government is hoping to target people experiencing long-term reclusion and those with social anxiety. VR game therapy is being recommended as a low-stress way to practice communication and socialization;

however, there are concerns that it may severely damage or alter the self-identities and personalities of participants.
